**ORCH digest — ProdKit.AI iOS v1: AC-lock RATIFIED**

The PM delivered acceptance criteria for all 11 tickets and requested ratification — the gate I set before any engineer writes code. I reviewed the full AC doc against your spec and the board norms.

**Ratified** (`ce86a41a` → PM, `c6c272cc` → TL): The AC set is strong — every ticket has testable ACs plus a TDD failing-test-first criterion; T3 is correctly spike-first (S1–S3 before T7 is sized); the T8 escalation policy, T6 card order, and T9 chat semantics all match your spec exactly. Bound three conditions: SEC must review the new mobile data endpoint, live dashboard updates must default to SSE push (not an 8s poll — per the event-driven norm), and the T1 label was corrected to reflect that the auth gate already landed @5c29124.

**One crossed-wire I caught and resolved:** my ratification and PM's latest amendment passed each other in flight, leaving **two conflicting directives for T4 (the mobile data API)** — mine said keep `/api/pulse` direct, PM's reverted to a thin `/api/v1/dashboard`. Left unresolved, TL would have dispatched an engineer to build the wrong thing. I sent a converging ruling (`fbb626fb` → PM, `79b2b9f6` → TL): build the thin `/api/v1/dashboard` (decoupled, coherent with the `/api/v1/` chat+stream namespace) but have it **reuse** `/api/pulse`'s data internally (DRY, no duplicate logic, no overfetch). That ends the thrash with one source of truth.

